    <bpmn:process id="W_W3847" name="W3847. Selling Quality Assurance, Mystery Shopping &amp; Customer Interaction Audit" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: QA cycle; quality concern
Frequency: Continuous + periodic
Volume: Selling-quality program across ~200 stores
Owner: Sales Enablement / Insights
Participants: Sales Enablement, Insights (links to VS-44), Store Ops (links to VS-07), L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4), CX (links to VS-13), Compliance (links to VS-22), Mystery Shopping vendor
Source: workflow W3847 — Selling Quality Assurance, Mystery Shopping &amp; Customer Interaction Audit</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3847_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3847_Lane1" name="Sales Enablement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3847_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3847_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3847_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3847_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3847_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3847_Start3" name="QA cycle; quality concern">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3847_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3847_Task4" name="Sales Enablement/Insights design the selling-quality program: mystery shopping…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sales Enablement/Insights design the selling-quality program: mystery shopping (scenario-based visits per store/department), customer-interaction audits (POS transaction review, recorded-call review for call center links to VS-13.1), and a quality rubric (greeting, needs-discovery, product knowledge, attach, loyalty, closing)
Responsible (R): Sales Enablement / Insights
Accountable (A): Sales Enablement Lead
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3847_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3847_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3847_Task5" name="Sales Enablement/Store-Ops execute mystery shopping/audits, score…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sales Enablement/Store-Ops execute mystery shopping/audits, score stores/associates, and feed findings into coaching (links to W3836), recognition (links to W3838), and corrective action
Responsible (R): Sales Enablement / Store Ops / Insights
Accountable (A): Sales Enablement Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3847_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3847_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3847_Task6" name="Sales Enablement/Insights correlate selling-quality scores with selling KPIs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sales Enablement/Insights correlate selling-quality scores with selling KPIs (basket, attach, conversion, CSAT — links to W3849/VS-13) and report quality posture to commercial/store leadership
Responsible (R): Sales Enablement / Analytics
Accountable (A): Sales Enablement Lead / COO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3847_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3847_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3847_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3847_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3847_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-88 (ensure selling-quality &amp; training integrity.) | - operational: varied scenarios and multiple signals; operational: coaching linkage
Owner: Sales Enablement / Insights</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
